  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nToday through Saturday, an upper level ridge moves across the \nregion bringing warmer and drier weather for a couple days. Gusty \nSE wind is expected ahead of a cold front Saturday night, and \nmight get high enough to reach Lake Wind Advisory criteria.\nCurrently this is just happening next to the dam, but could \neasily expand in future forecasts. \n\nSaturday night onward, conditions cool off with a cold front \ninitially saturday night into mid-day Sunday as zonal flow returns\ninitially. Another brief shortwave will pull rain showers across \nthe region as well. But then, temps gradually meander upward into \nthe 80s for highs by Wednesday and Thursday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo changes to NBM tonight.",
